Probe user_regs_struct with <sys/types.h> instead of glibc's <bits/types.h>.

The x86 peekfd gate checks struct user_regs_struct in <sys/user.h>, but the
probe also includes <bits/types.h>, a glibc-internal header musl does not
have. The probe fails to compile, every member reads "no", and peekfd is
silently left out on x86_64 and i686. <sys/user.h> declares the struct on its
own; <sys/types.h> is the portable header for whatever it might need.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@
 		struct user_regs_struct.rdi,
 		struct user_regs_struct.rsi,
 		struct user_regs_struct.rdx], [],[],
-    [#include <bits/types.h>
+    [#include <sys/types.h>
      #include <sys/user.h>])
 AC_CHECK_MEMBERS([struct pt_regs.orig_gpr3,
 		struct pt_regs.gpr], [],[], [#include <linux/ptrace.h>])
